[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="IslandField" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/world/SCRIPT_island_field.gd" id="1_field"]

; SCENE_test_zone_W2's island field: a single SOLID hub island, nothing else.
;
; Three deltas from ISLANDFIELD_default.tres, and only three:
;   * ruin_enabled = true -> the RUIN ENTRANCES' clearings, each levelled to the
;     plane the ruin's own model says it meets the ground on, with the hill easing
;     back round it. OFF in the script, so this preset is the only world that
;     levels any; SCENE_island_0 (and W2, which shares this file) stand
;     PREFAB_ruin_entrance_type1 in every one through SCRIPT_ruin_site.gd. The
;     disc's radius and height are copies of the model's and are left at the
;     script defaults deliberately — one copy in the field, checked against the
;     mesh by tests/TEST_ruin_site.gd, rather than two that could disagree with
;     each other. See docs/DOC_ruin_site.md.
;
;     A RING OF SEVEN, not the one near the pod (ruin_ring_count = 7): entrances
;     at even bearings 360/7 apart round the hub's centre, 800 m out
;     (ruin_ring_radius 0.64 of 1250 m), the first on bearing 0.75 degrees in the
;     field's XZ frame — compass 90.75, due east — and every door facing the
;     centre. Each may slide up to 80 m along its own bearing to find ground it can
;     be levelled on with no more than 5.5 m of earthwork; on this seed none goes
;     further than 30 m. The spin and the radius were searched for, not chosen:
;     between the course inside and the coast outside, only spins from 0.50 to 1.00
;     degrees stand all seven. tests/PROBE_ruin_ring.gd prints the ring and the
;     search. The ingress / egress test layout; ruin_ring_count = 0 puts back the
;     single entrance near the pod.
;   * satellite_density_near/far = 0 -> every non-hub lattice cell rolls empty in
;     island_field._cell_island(), so the world is the anchor hub and pure void.
;     The sibling hubs on the 12-cell lattice sit 10.8 km out, far past W2's
;     view_distance + hub_radius reach (~4.85 km), so only the core hub renders.
;   * coast_jagged = true with coast_irregularity = 0.2 -> a JAGGED shore that is
;     still guaranteed hole-free and scatter-free. In jagged mode the wobble is a
;     function of BEARING from the hub centre only, so the land is the star domain
;     {distance <= R(angle)}: along every ray out from the centre the mask crosses
;     zero exactly once, so there are no detached land specks off the rim and no
;     void lagoons biting into it — the coast is serrated but the island is one
;     solid connected piece. coast_jag_scale sets how fine the serrations are.
;     zone/sand placement stay clear of the jaggiest inward notch automatically
;     (their coast margins subtract coast_irregularity).
;
; Everything else is copied verbatim from ISLANDFIELD_default.tres so the hub's
; terrain, golf course, build pads and cliffs are unchanged.

